Scope: synthetic DOM, RAF clock and in-memory transport tests of actual frontend
classes. This log does not establish a real browser, authentication, database or
Socket.IO network playthrough.

Baseline contract migration:
- All 9 original C03/C04/C08 behavioral cases remain in frontend-lifecycle.spec.ts.
- GameplayService.start now requires the server's validated v1 ReadyMessage, so
  each start receives a canonicalReady fixture with mode, side, generation and
  captured core state. The old payload-less call no longer starts a match.
- C04 events execute KeyboardController -> OnlineSession -> MatchInput. The legacy
  Bar string encoder is no longer used by production GameplayService.
- Opposite movement still must be neutral. DTO sequence advances on refresh, so
  the comparison asserts movement plus runtime-valid DTOs instead of requiring
  identical sequence metadata. Movement+Power asserts both up=true and a new
  actionId in the same packet.
- Replacing a session may send one intentional neutral teardown packet. Calls
  are cleared immediately after replacement; invoking captured OLD callbacks
  must produce no packets and must not add a RAF. The replacement's first packet
  must use its new generation and neutral movement.
- No behavioral case was skipped, removed, or given a weakened success outcome.

Environment: Node 18.20.8, existing backend Jest/ts-jest; commands run in backend.

