Fixture correction (not a production defect): one intermediate 13-case run also
failed the 80ms ack check because swapping Jest's global performance object did
not consistently replace the module's clock reference. The fixture now installs
and restores performance.now on the existing object; the unchanged 80ms assertion
passed. That intermediate run was 10 passed/3 failed, exit 1, 1.053 s.

Accepted production fixes (implemented by the root agent):
- Initial and received network snapshots use captureSnapshot to own their data.
- Disposed status/motion callbacks return without changing the former owner's UI.

